SEP mockup tests
================

For details: https://wiki.gsi.de/NustarDAQ/SEPMockupTests

Run example with:

 ./sep_mockup.bash

Setup
-----

3 crates, syncronised with White Rabbit timestamps.  Each with:

- MVLC    (Controller)
- TRLO II (Rrigger logic)
- VETAR   (White rabbit time)
- VFTX    (high-precision TDCs)

Middle crate makes trigger decision, left and right crate take triggers.

Plots page 1 (corr)
-------------------

Monitoring plots.

- SC : sync check values:
  Varying master start length distributed to all systems.

- VFTX : high-precision TDC, driven by 200 MHz clock from WR (VETARs)

- WR : white rabbit timestamps.
  lm = left-middle, lr = left-right, rm = right-middle

  Third and fourth row are same.  Third row has minimum bin width hint.

Plots page 2 (extra)
--------------------

Additional plots.

- Triggers taken.

- Sync check values for middle and right system.

- VFTX times, full time vs. channel.

- VFTX multiplicity, middle system.

- Several more VFTX plots...
